From d7df6ee355c9be44b00f69852e9def786d603705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:32:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] virtio-gpu: fenced flushes of a GL scanout complete when
 the frame is shown

A RESOURCE_FLUSH of a blob scanout is answered as soon as it is queued,
so a guest has no page-flip completion: it can't tell when the host took
its frame, when the previous buffer is free, or where the host's vblank
is. A fenced flush is now deferred to the fence queue and answered when
the display reports the frame shown (new GraphicHwOps.frame_shown). The
GTK EGL display reports it at the latch point of the refresh the frame
makes - the host vblank plus the pacing phase of the previous patch, the
first one the frame is at most QEMU_GTK_LATCH_SLACK_US (250 us: the trip from the guest) late for -
once its draw is done. Displays that don't report frames answer when the
renderer unblocks after the draw. A 50 ms timer answers fences a display
never reports (a hidden window); after three such timeouts in a row the
device stops deferring until the display reports again.

Unfenced flushes are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
